---
/* The site's mark: a ring for the watching, a dot for the record being kept.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The same two shapes the favicon has always drawn, promoted to the page — one
   drawing, three sizes: the tab, the top bar, and the cover's plate. It took
   over the plate when the owner retired the Persian-script covermark
   (2026-08-13) and asked for a mark instead.

   Inline SVG rather than an <img> of the favicon, because the favicon cannot
   read the page's tokens and this can: the ring is `currentColor` — the ink of
   wherever it sits — and the dot is the accent role, so the mark follows both
   schemes and the theme toggle for free. The favicon repeats the two accent
   hexes by hand for exactly this reason; this file never has to.

   No intrinsic size. The caller sizes it in its own stylesheet
   (`:global(svg)` from the parent scope), because 1em in a top bar and a
   plate on a cover are layout facts about those places, not about the mark.

   aria-hidden always: everywhere it appears, text beside it already names the
   site, and a screen reader announcing "image" between the name and its gloss
   would be decoration read aloud. */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
  <circle class="ring" cx="32" cy="32" r="25" stroke-width="7" />
  <circle class="dot" cx="32" cy="32" r="9" />
</svg>

<style>
  .ring {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
  }

  .dot {
    fill: var(--accent);
    stroke: none;
  }
</style>
